    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 2 part 4b P4 negative.log (specs/0020-validation-and-conditional-
    # formatting.md, "P4": "the negative log through the binary with every
    # refusal of this part reachable through the binary run once (the fixture
    # cases of P1 to P3, and the at-call refusals named as not reachable, since
    # their inputs are the tool's constants)").
    # The gate's host debug binary copied into a detached worktree of the phase
    # commit and checked against gate.log's hash, run on fictional packages this
    # log builds from the phase commit's template files: P1's five validation
    # fixtures and P2's six conditional format fixtures, the latter run through
    # both --cf-sample and --scale-sample as P2's and P3's logs ran them. The
    # template's worksheet holds an empty sheetData alone, so M is 0:
    #
    # (V) --validate-sample (P1's V0 to V4): the list on A1, the whole number on
    #     B1:B2, the list removed again in memory:
    #       V0 the bare template: exit 0, its line;
    #       V1 a dataValidations holding one type="none" validation on A1, the
    #          sample's first cell: the overlap message;
    #       V2 the same validation on D1, the control for V1: exit 0, its line;
    #       V3 two empty <dataValidations/>: the two-container message;
    #       V4 one empty <dataValidations/>, the control for V3: exit 0, its line.
    # (C) --cf-sample (P2's C0 to C5): a style, a greater-than rule on A1:C1 and
    #     an expression rule on A2, the A2 format removed again in memory:
    #       C0 the bare template: exit 0, its line;
    #       C1 a conditionalFormatting on A2 whose dataBar rule holds an extLst:
    #          the extension message, at the in-memory removal, the output removed;
    #       C2 the same element on D1, the control for C1: exit 0, its line;
    #       C3 a conditionalFormatting on D1 whose expression rule's priority is
    #          "high": the sqref-or-attribute message, at the read;
    #       C4 the same rule with priority "1", the control for C3: exit 0;
    #       C5 the styles part with two empty <dxfs/>: the two-dxfs message, at
    #          the differential style's call.
    # (S) --scale-sample (P3's run of P2's fixtures): three visual rules on
    #     A1:A3, B1:B3 and C1:C3, no style, nothing removed: S3 (C3's fixture)
    #     refused with the sqref-or-attribute message; S1, S2 and S5 (C1's, C2's
    #     and C5's fixtures) not refused, each running to the line its input
    #     implies, since the sample removes nothing and adds no style.
    # A refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed source
    # holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's fifteen messages, read
    # from the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here
    # and those the log states unreachable, with the reason for each; and usage
    # shapes, one per sample.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4b P4 from P3's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p4b-p3/negative.log; its change list AN to AT is there),
    # with P1's and P2's fixtures and lines (their logs, records/logs/m2p4b-p1/
    # and m2p4b-p2/negative.log). Generated from P3's script by <home>/.cache/
    # emend-build/m2p4b-p4/gen/negative.py, every replacement asserted to occur
    # once; grepped for P3's tokens in every form (p3, the P3 subjects and
    # commits, c98838a0). What differs, and why:
    #  BA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are part 4b P4's. The base is P3's record commit ("M2 part 4b P3
    #      record:"); the doc commit and the three code commits by their full P4
    #      subjects, so the roles run from <phase commit>~0 to ~4. The spec pin
    #      is the committed blob 2b4afb62 of P4's doc commit, which holds every
    #      ruling of P1 to P3; the working file is hashed and printed, never
    #      asserted. The status pattern allows this phase's log directory, its
    #      records (the three sample pairs m2p4b-p4-<sample>-, the open check
    #      m2p4b-open- and the size record size-m2p4b-) and planning's spec.
    #  BB. The messages block is the part's whole fifteen, NO_AREA to
    #      RULE_UNPARSED. Reached: VALIDATION_OVERLAP, TWO_VALIDATIONS (P1's),
    #      RULE_EXTENDED, TWO_DXFS and RULE_UNPARSED (P2's, the last also
    #      through --scale-sample). Stated unreachable, each with its reason:
    #      the other ten, every at-call refusal among them, since each sample's
    #      inputs are the tool's constants. Each message is also looked for in
    #      the committed spec, which now names all fifteen.
    #  BC. The fixtures are P1's five and P2's six, built by one generator
    #      from the phase commit's template files; the lines are P1's, P2's and
    #      P3's for the same fixtures.
    #  BD. The usage shapes: one per sample.
    #
    # Usage: m2p4b-p4-negative.sh <phase commit> [<gate log> [<gate build dir>]]
    # > <file outside the tree>; the caller moves the output to
    # records/logs/m2p4b-p4/negative.log.
    set -uo pipefail
